{"id":"2174734858","kind":"answer","title":"死记硬背还是有用的吧！？","author":"Thoughts Memo","original_authors":["Thoughts Memo"],"original_source_urls":[],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2021-10-17","updated":"2021-10-17","votes":23,"comment_count":3,"minutes":1,"chars":431,"keywords":["学习动机","记忆干扰","渐进阅读","自由学习","间隔重复"],"summary":"原文： 死记硬背（填鸭式学习） - 知乎 (zhihu.com) 死记硬背 是一种在匆忙中集中学习的形式（如考试前的最后一个晚上）。 死记硬背 会导致记忆的连贯性 [1] 差。连贯性低意味着你可以通过考试，但仍然知之甚少。 死记硬背可以帮助你通过考试，但它也是非常有害的。它真的会伤害你的大脑或健康。它会影响你对学习的热爱 [2…","question_detail_html":"我非常不擅长，也不喜欢理解课文内容背后的思想，东西几乎是能用背就背，用背就能考好的科目我最喜欢，讨厌理解！我觉得了解了也没意义。<br/>每次看到大家都批评死记硬背的填鸭教育我表示压力好大，这是我唯一擅长的读书方式，也只想考试考好，管他未来用不用得到，难道死记硬背真的不好吗？","zhihu_url":"https://www.zhihu.com/question/38464100/answer/2174734858","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<blockquote data-pid=\"W8wnYTj7\">原文：<a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"360416156\" href=\"#/post/360416156\">死记硬背（填鸭式学习） - 知乎 (zhihu.com)</a></blockquote><p data-pid=\"dnibkF6d\"><b>死记硬背</b>是一种在匆忙中集中学习的形式（如考试前的最后一个晚上）。<b>死记硬背</b>会导致记忆的连贯性<sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>差。连贯性低意味着你可以通过考试，但仍然知之甚少。</p><p data-pid=\"up4UfMNF\">死记硬背可以帮助你通过考试，但它也是非常有害的。它真的会伤害你的大脑或健康。它会影响你对学习的热爱<sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>。它产生的短期记忆，会通过干扰<sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>很快被遗忘。但是，如果对同一学习材料反复使用，<b>死记硬背</b>会导致毒性记忆<sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>。只有当你现在需要快速掌握大量知识一段时间，<b>死记硬背</b>才是有用的。你千万不要在晚上死记硬背。</p><p data-pid=\"_mokK294\">另请参考：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"iCsxTiMV\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/50_bad_habits_learned_at_school\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">在学校学到的50个坏习惯</a></li><li data-pid=\"ZgmU7La0\">语义学习<sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>(与死记硬背相反)</li><li data-pid=\"o2v3kw56\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Serendipitous_impact_of_mindless_cramming\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">死记硬背是如何帮助发展渐进阅读的？</a></li><li data-pid=\"y4CUuhO0\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://twitter.com/guillemlearner/status/1316811830669512706/photo/1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">幽默</a></li></ul><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 一致性与连贯性(Consistency vs Coherence) <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"264327134\" href=\"#/post/264327134\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 学习的乐趣 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1578551193\" href=\"#/post/1578551193\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 干扰 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"269974053\" href=\"#/post/269974053\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 毒性记忆 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"67390960\" href=\"#/post/67390960\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 语义学习 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"266922623\" href=\"#/post/266922623\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"67390960","title":"9 毒性记忆","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":227,"minutes":24,"reason":"本回答Level 1 核心引用"},{"id":"266922623","title":"语义学习","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":92,"minutes":6,"reason":"本回答Level 1 核心引用"},{"id":"264327134","title":"一致性与连贯性","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":60,"minutes":2,"reason":"本回答Level 1 核心引用"},{"id":"269974053","title":"干扰","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":28,"minutes":1,"reason":"本回答Level 1 核心引用"},{"id":"360416156","title":"死记硬背（填鸭式学习）","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":49,"minutes":1,"reason":"本回答Level 3 引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"281085595","title":"不要在没有理解之前就去记忆","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":158,"minutes":9,"reason":"延伸深读 · Piotr Wozniak"},{"id":"306014650","title":"老汤比喻","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":36,"minutes":3,"reason":"延伸深读 · Piotr Wozniak"},{"id":"295053968","title":"无语义学习","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":58,"minutes":2,"reason":"延伸深读 · Piotr Wozniak"},{"id":"265081034","title":"遗忘机制","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":59,"minutes":8,"reason":"延伸深读 · Piotr Wozniak"},{"id":"273225977","title":"学习的基本规律","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":137,"minutes":4,"reason":"延伸深读 · Piotr Wozniak"}],"rec_answers":[{"id":"2425589576","title":"有没有人真的不适合应试教育？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":1108,"minutes":7,"reason":"相似问答 · 1108 赞同"},{"id":"2021597263521129478","title":"高效学习者们是如何锻炼记忆力的？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":366,"minutes":25,"reason":"相似问答 · 366 赞同"},{"id":"2752308135","title":"如何看待应试教育中的死记硬背？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":95,"minutes":4,"reason":"相似问答 · 95 赞同"},{"id":"2155395768","title":"快速地死记硬背和慢慢地理解应该选哪个？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":19,"minutes":18,"reason":"相似问答 · 19 赞同"},{"id":"1568731419","title":"高中生因写作业时间长，没有多的时间复习巩固，导致作业不会写且写的更慢的恶性循环该如何解决?","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":15,"minutes":1,"reason":"相似问答 · 15 赞同"}]}